# Lab 1: Controllers to Minimal APIs
# Same calls before and after the migration. The responses should not change,
# except where Lab 1 changes them on purpose (contracts, version headers).
@host = https://localhost:7001
@ticketId = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111

### List tickets (check the api-supported-versions header after Lab 1)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/tickets

### Get one ticket (after Lab 1: commentCount instead of an embedded comments array)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/tickets/{{ticketId}}

### Create a ticket
POST {{host}}/api/v1/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Printer on fire",
  "description": "Literally.",
  "priority": "Urgent",
  "requesterId": "bob"
}

### Overposting: try to assign and close your own ticket on create
# Before Lab 1 the domain model binds these. After, the contract ignores them.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Please fix",
  "description": "Sneaky fields.",
  "priority": "Low",
  "requesterId": "mallory",
  "assigneeId": "mallory",
  "status": "Closed"
}

### List comments
GET {{host}}/api/v1/tickets/{{ticketId}}/comments

### Add a comment
POST {{host}}/api/v1/tickets/{{ticketId}}/comments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "authorId": "dana", "body": "Looking into it." }

### A version that doesn't exist (404)
GET {{host}}/api/v2/tickets

### The OpenAPI document (after Lab 1)
GET {{host}}/openapi/v1.json
